{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1126157-new-storyteller-looking-for-some-advice-and-story-ideas-for-his-second-mage-chronicle","id":1126157,"title":"New Storyteller looking for some advice and story ideas for his second mage chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-07T20:51:57-07:00","id":1126157,"title":"New Storyteller looking for some advice and story ideas for his second mage chronicle","content":"so we just finished our first chronicle and I'm struggling with ideas for a second. first some backstory for the characters involved and what they've done so far.<br /> <br /> the awakned we have 3 players<br /> <br /> the first is a character named Killian he's an orphan mage who channels his magic through crafting objects that he channels his magic through, he also decided his avatar should be it's own personaltiy that talks to him<br /> we have a nother character named skuldifer who's a verbena priest who worships the norse gods he makes sacraficees and calls upon the norse gods to grant him powers<br /> and we have amanda whos a sister of ether a mad scietist<br /> <br /> the first campaign centered around a group of very young but powerful mages being controled/manipulated by a vampire. the idea was to create a local reality free of paradox by haveing the city be teleported to a node in the middle of the ocean yes high corespondence was involved. to enact some crazy vampire plan to plunge the world into eternal darkness, he was a lasombra with dominate he used memory manipulation to make them willingly follow him. they killed the vampire and befriended the mages at the end of the campaign they put the town back leaving just their base floating on the ocean node, the wreck of the titanic specificaly. then to show the full consequences of paradox at the end i hade a paradox spirit put them on trial sentenced the corespondence mage to death and the player characters killian and skuldifer who helped in the ritual to put the town back got crushed to near death. thenhealed by amanda's mentor a famous awakned doctor useing a vat of stemcells and a tesla coil that channels lightning tass.<br /> <br /> this was our first chronicle and our first time playing mage. and i don't know what to do with the second campaign or how to actually deal with the cabals conflicting ideals we've mostly ignored or hand waved away their conflicting belifs creating paradox for eachother, amanda specificaly. and i need some advice of how we can explaine that. i also haveing storryteller/writers block on what to do for their next adventure. would apreciate some advice<br /> <br /> ps i apologise if this is in the wrong thread or something this is my first time posting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13303,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13303-jay15951","user":"Jay15951","date":". 08-07-2017, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13303-jay15951","name":"Jay15951","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13303_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T03:52:12-07:00","id":1126243,"title":"","content":"Regarding conflict. That's a real pity you hand waved that. A lot of the fun of a tradition campaign is in the arguments that occur from differences in approach and views to magic. This would not create paradox, it would just create conflict.<br /> <br /> The Etherites might try to explain away the other's magic using what she understands to be science, while the Verbena could be at odds with the Etherites dismissal of the old gods, saying that she is dismissing that which she cannot understand.<br /> This is to be encouraged, and perhaps even rewarded with experience.<br /> <br /> Regarding campaigns, I'd say deal with the aftermath of this stories events.<br /> How did it affect each Mages homelife?<br /> Is the technocracy investigating this?<br /> What other traditions might be getting involved?<br /> What about other mages of their own traditions?<br /> -would the verbena wish to repair the damage caused?<br /> -would the etherites yearn to study it?<br /> Are the spirits pissed off?<br /> Have the nephandi been using these events to their advantage?<br /> <br /> So many factions to consider, but at the heart of it, you should always keep in mind what your players would want to achieve. Power? Influence? Control? Peace? Understanding? Or maybe just freedom?<br /> <br /> Talk to them. Get feedback from their experience. See what they think their characters are now trying to achieve and let this become the central theme of your next story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 08-08-2017, 06:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T09:42:49-07:00","id":1127177,"title":"","content":"Another possibility, if you don't mind some crazy stuff, make it that the massive Correspondence ritual create a little tear in the Gaunlet and some stuff from the Deep Umbra (I don't remember if that was the deep space place) came from it. It could be a creature that starts to infect people and creating some xenomorph like creatures. This would, of course, atract the atention of the Technocracy, specifically the Void Engineers. Depending of the level of the threat this could force all the groups to work together to preserve the secrecy. Still nothing prevents the Void Engineers to double cross the group as soon as everything is under control. You could make that the transformation of the victims is permanent or that it is reversable. One way or another, it would be consequences and some plan to do.<br /> <br /> Just a thing I thought while reading this... I got some really crazy ideas sometimes. XD<br /> <br /> Good luck! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13478-drakeepsilon","name":"DrakeEpsilon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13478_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T14:02:11-07:00","id":1127310,"title":"","content":"thanks both of you for the advice i think I've come up with a good idea combining your 2 posts with some of my own idea's. The technocracy are going to be investigating &quot;the scar&quot; and stumble across our main characters. while at the same time a group of nephandi cultist specifically K'llasshaa are going to use &quot;the scar&quot; to tear a hole in the gauntlet in order to release a lovecraftian demon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13303,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13303-jay15951","user":"Jay15951","date":". 08-10-2017, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":